---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Terms of service — CanYouDo?">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of service</h1>
      <p class="hint">Last updated: 8 August 2026 · These terms are written in plain English on purpose.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:36px">1. What CanYouDo? is</h2>
      <p>CanYouDo? ("we", "us"), operating at canyoudo.uk, is an <strong>online introduction service</strong>: a platform (an online notice board) that connects customers seeking cleaning services with independent cleaners offering them, and provides booking, messaging, notification and rating tools.</p>
      <p><strong>We are not a cleaning company, employment agency, or employer.</strong> We do not provide cleaning services, supervise work, or guarantee outcomes. The cleaning contract is formed directly between the customer and the cleaner.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">2. Independent service providers</h2>
      <p>Cleaners on CanYouDo? are self-employed, independent service providers. They set their own availability, accept or decline work at their discretion, and are responsible for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>their own <strong>public liability insurance</strong> (details they provide — insurer, policy number and expiry — are displayed to build trust, but we do not verify or underwrite cover);</li>
        <li>their own tax and National Insurance;</li>
        <li>the standard and safety of their own work.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">3. Payments</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Customers pay CanYouDo? an <strong>introduction fee of £5 per booked hour</strong> when booking, online.</li>
        <li>Customers pay the cleaner <strong>£15 per hour directly</strong> (cash or bank transfer) — we do not collect, hold or process the cleaner's payment.</li>
        <li>Introduction fees are refundable if a booking is cancelled by either party before it takes place.</li>
        <li>CanYouDo? pays cleaners optional monthly quality bonuses from its own funds, based on the published, measurable criteria.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">4. Customers' responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide all cleaning products and equipment, safe and fit for use.</li>
        <li>Provide a safe working environment and accurate access instructions.</li>
        <li>Pay the cleaner in full on the day of the visit.</li>
        <li>Rate visits honestly — ratings determine cleaner bonuses.</li>
        <li>Insurance for the property and its contents remains the customer's responsibility.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">5. Cleaners' responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Keep profile, availability and insurance details accurate and current.</li>
        <li>Arrive on time, clean the areas requested, and follow reasonable instructions.</li>
        <li>Communicate promptly through the portal if plans change.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">6. Liability</h2>
      <p>Because we are an introduction service only, we are not liable for the acts, omissions, or quality of work of cleaners, nor for loss or damage arising during a clean. Claims relating to a clean should be addressed between customer and cleaner (and the cleaner's insurer where relevant). Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law. Our total liability to any user is limited to the introduction fees they paid us in the previous 12 months.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">7. Fair use and removal</h2>
      <p>We may remove users who provide false information (including false insurance details), behave abusively, repeatedly cancel, or attempt to game ratings or bonuses. Circumventing the platform to avoid introduction fees after being introduced here may result in removal.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">8. The booking system</h2>
      <p>Bookings, reminders and notifications are managed by our AI-assisted booking system. Automated emails are sent when bookings are made, confirmed, changed or cancelled. Automated checks may flag unusual bookings for human review. The system assists — decisions about accepting work always rest with the cleaner.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">9. Contact</h2>
      <p>Customer service: <a href="mailto:hello@canyoudo.uk">hello@canyoudo.uk</a>. These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
